                <pb facs="0253" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg153"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/24053: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-22T09:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">May 22, 1920—9
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:32 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>240. Entire press today publishes official bulletin issued from General Obregón’s
                    headquarters stating that President Carranza and six of his followers, names
                    unknown, were killed at 1 o’clock yesterday morning near Necaxa, State of Puebla
                    in an attack on his party made by Rodolfo Herrero an ex-Federal belonging to the
                    command of General Mariel who accompanied President Carranza.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
